.\" man/man3/Docv::Roff::Numeric.3cr
.\" Generated by docv gen-cr from README.md and the doc comments; regenerate instead of editing.
.TH "Docv::Roff::Numeric" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::Roff::Numeric \- roff numeric expressions in basic units, as on a terminal device: one character cell is 24 units wide, one line (\fB\%v\fR) is 40 units high.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv"\fR
.sp
\fBmodule Docv::Roff::Numeric\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
roff numeric expressions in basic units, as on a terminal device: one
character cell is 24 units wide, one line (\fB\%v\fR) is 40 units high.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBCOLUMN = 24\fR
Units per character column.
.TP 4
\fBLINE = 40\fR
Units per output line.
.TP 4
\fBMAX_EXTENT = 1000\fR
Largest column or line count a conversion yields; larger values from
page typos would otherwise allocate enormous lines.
.TP 4
\fBSCALE\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
SCALE = {
  \(aqu\(aq => 1.0,
  \(aqn\(aq => 24.0,
  \(aqm\(aq => 24.0,
  \(aqi\(aq => 240.0,
  \(aqc\(aq => 240.0 / 2.54,
  \(aqp\(aq => 240.0 / 72.0,
  \(aqP\(aq => 40.0,
  \(aqv\(aq => 40.0,
  \(aqM\(aq => 0.24,
  \(aqs\(aq => 1.0,
  \(aqz\(aq => 1.0,
  \(aqf\(aq => 65536.0,
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Basic units per scale indicator.
.RE
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.TP 4
\fBdef self.columns(text : String, unit : Char = \(aqn\(aq) : Int32 | Nil\fR
Evaluates \fItext\fR to columns (rounded) with default scale \fIunit\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.eval(text : String, unit : Char = \(aqu\(aq) : Int64 | Nil\fR
Evaluates \fItext\fR fully; \fB\%nil\fR when it is not a valid expression.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.lines(text : String, unit : Char = \(aqv\(aq) : Int32 | Nil\fR
Evaluates \fItext\fR to output lines (rounded) with default scale \fIunit\fR.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.parse(text : String, pos : Int32, unit : Char) : Tuple(Int64 | Nil, Int32)\fR
Parses an expression at \fIpos\fR; returns the value (or \fB\%nil\fR) and the
position after it. Operators apply left to right without precedence.
.SH "DEFINED IN"
src/docv/roff/numeric.cr
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR "Docv::Roff" (3cr),
.BR "docv" (7cr)
